{"title":"07 Visualization","description":"Render paper figures from computed frames without opening windows.","steps":[{"file":"src/delware_speech/visualization.py","line":24,"title":"Headless by design","description":"`matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")` at import time — figures are files, never windows. Importing this module anywhere (tests, CLI, notebooks) is safe without a display."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/visualization.py","line":28,"title":"Paper palettes","description":"Four cluster colors and the diagnosis palette shared by every figure — the visual identity matches the paper's aesthetics."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/visualization.py","line":32,"title":"Figure 3a — clustered heatmap","description":"`plot_cluster_correlation_matrix` reorders the correlation matrix by cluster membership (lines 39–41) so domains appear as blocks, then draws a diverging heatmap at 300 dpi."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/visualization.py","line":67,"title":"Figure 3b — t-SNE","description":"`plot_tsne_clusters` projects the same feature-correlation space to 2D, colored by cluster. Line 77 guards perplexity to the valid range for small feature counts; `random_state=42` keeps it deterministic."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/visualization.py","line":107,"title":"Importance bar chart","description":"`plot_feature_importance` — horizontal bars of the top-N Gini scores with value labels. Only called when `--importance` ran in the same invocation (see tour 01)."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/visualization.py","line":138,"title":"Figure 5 — violins","description":"`plot_violin_features` lays one violin per feature across diagnostic groups on an automatic n×3 grid (lines 150–155); missing features are skipped, unused axes switched off."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/visualization.py","line":186,"title":"Figure 6 — MoCA regressions","description":"`plot_cognitive_regressions` — seaborn regplot per feature vs MoCA with the correlation r annotated in each panel title (line 221). Panels with <5 complete pairs are silently skipped (line 209)."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/visualization.py","line":244,"title":"Figure 4 — task radars","description":"`plot_task_radar` — one polar subplot per picture task (Cookie/Cat/Rockwell), features z-scored across the whole dataset first (lines 275–278) so the radar scale is comparable; group means drawn per diagnosis."}]}